{"baseRefName":"codex/research-online-c1-source-reconcile","body":"The source logarithmic FTL upper bound does not by itself produce an ordinary fixed-comparator limit. For the existing initial-half strict-past squared-loss FTL, this package proves an exact converse: on one all-time unit observation stream, the literal all-comparator finite nonpositive limit predicate holds iff the empirical mean converges to one feasible real value. It also constructs one explicit bounded dyadic stream, proves its support and two actual mean subsequence limits (2/3 and1/3), and proves that the SAME FTL has upper NoRegret and true feasible-best regret/T tending0 while fixed-zero regret/T has no finite real limit. No convergence, support or regret oracle is assumed.\n\nThe four endpoints are derived reconciliation results for Orabona arXiv:1912.13213v10 (2026-06-21), printed2/4/6, rather than four printed theorems. The pinned ordinary-lim display, existing upper-epsilon predicate and separately proposed source correction remain distinct. The dyadic recursion fixes d0=0 and d(n+1)=1-d(floor(n/2)); prefixes use t<T and the natural subsequence horizons4^(n+1)-1 and2*4^n-1. Initial learner output remains1/2 and later predictions use strict past. There is no contradiction to the source4+4logT upper bound and no stochastic, minimax or all-algorithm impossibility claim.\n\nEleven public canaries instantiate all four endpoints and check actual observations0,1,1,0, predictions1/2,0,1/2,2/3, best regrets0,1/4,3/4,5/6 and fixed-zero R3/3=-1/6. Validation evidence includes focused builds,4 whole-type proof VALUE witnesses,28 standard-only axiom outputs,15 fences,19 required direct VALUE pairs in a selected24-node graph, combined root/Tests/full harness (472 tests,7 skips), two nonempty committed-HEAD contributor gates and an owned shadow. The applicable clean local site preserves10964 COMPLETE shared registry records and adds exactly4 PUBLIC production theorems plus1 PUBLIC supporting definition, alongside8 explicitly source-private helpers; those helpers are not public instantiable endpoints. Ten current original reader/catalogue images receive separate formalizer and source-reviewer inspection. Exact receipts are in runs/online-ftl-obstruction-20261009. D4 v1 implicit-zero inference failure is retained; v2 supplies explicit realzero without modifying the frozen statement or earlier proofs. Initial registry-count check1 omitted private inventory; evidence-only v2 retains alloldrecords and separately counts public/private identities, without altering proof/reader/registry code. RAW output whitespace exceptions are separately bound; no production or contract exemption.\n\nDistinct automated decoder/reviewer roles disclose reused history; no human/external/absolute-blind/runtime-model attestation. Only these four derived obligations may close. Original16Chapter1 source objects/null unknown proof total, full Chapter1 reconciliation, other C1/C2, unenumerated C3-16 and necessary appendices remain required; the full-book Goal stays ACTIVE. Stacked on OPEN draft unmerged PR201 exact224927197e78e1330c4c93e84f9c69388d3027a7, base codex/research-online-c1-source-reconcile. Main/live unchanged; no merge/deployment. Contracts: docs/contracts/online-ftl-obstruction-v1. Evidence: runs/online-ftl-obstruction-20261009. The active worktree is retained for subsequent required work.\n","headRefName":"codex/research-online-ftl-obstruction","headRefOid":"fd797b5cabfe9257d4f5e1ad916a2e147a6dd819","isDraft":true,"mergedAt":null,"number":202,"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/actions/runs/37835170483/job/113510242986","name":"contributor-contract","startedAt":"2026-10-08T19:52:16Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"Contributor contract"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":